  "question": {
    "text": "Let one focus of the hyperbola $\\mathrm{H}: \\frac{\\mathrm{x}^2}{\\mathrm{a}^2}-\\frac{\\mathrm{y}^2}{\\mathrm{~b}^2}=1$ be at $(\\sqrt{10}, 0)$ and the corresponding directrix be $\\mathrm{x}=\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{10}}$. If e and $l$ respectively are the eccentricity and the length of the latus rectum of H , then $9\\left(\\mathrm{e}^2+l\\right)$ is equal to:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "CHeJz",
